==Problem description==
Diagnosing and fixing a problem with a Siemens inverter Sinamics 6SL3120-1TE23-0AA3 that has a faulty output phase
[[File:20240527 142820.jpg|thumb|Healthy phase measurement, (negative on + DC link and vice versa to all phases should read this value) Figure 1]]
[[File:20240527 142826.jpg|thumb|Dead phase measurement (figure 2)]]
[[File:20240527 143123.jpg|thumb|The IGBT model for this inverter (figure 3)]]

==Symptoms== 

*Open line or short circuit from DC link to one or more of the output phases. 
*Unstable operation of the motor, spins little bit and stops.
*

==Solution==

===Diagnostic Steps===

* First, check the IGBT 

* Place your red probe on - DC link, and the black all the phases individually, they should measure close to the value on figure 1
* Do the same with black probe on + DC link
* If you measure all the values to be the same, then you have another issue, the IGBT is healthy 
* If you measure OL or low/short on one of the phases, proceed to repair steps<br />

===Repair Steps===
Replace the IGBT (Figure 3) and make sure the driving circuit isn't damaged, if you have a healthy phase you can compare since they're identical, measure the optocouplers/diodes.

After replacement the inverter should work properly.